{
  "video_id": "1sLDUbV2QRk",
  "title": "Store an AI knowledge base 8x cheaper with TurboVec",
  "description": "Comment \"TURBO\" and I'll send you the link.\n\nThere's now a way to store an AI knowledge base eight times cheaper. If you build your own AI product, you keep a vector knowledge base on a server. Ten million documents take 31 gigabytes you pay for monthly. A free library called TurboVec, built on Google Research's TurboQuant algorithm, shrinks that to four gigabytes. Same answers, same accuracy, eight times cheaper server bill.\n\n#ai #rag #aitools #vectordatabase #machinelearning",
